() Tj T*
(TRACEABLE AI INTELLIGENCE INGESTION - ARCHITECTURE) Tj T*
(Implemented reference pipeline: Phase I acquisitions, Phase II freshness ingestion, Phase III grounded) Tj T*
(LLM extraction, Phase IV deterministic entity resolution, Phase V compliance controls. Production scale) Tj T*
(components below are designed, not load-tested locally.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Scale to 500,000+ startups, products and papers) Tj T*
(- Partition every work stream by \(source, shard hash of canonical URL or arXiv id\). Each partition is) Tj T*
(  an ordered, replayable task stream; no code change is needed to add shards.) Tj T*
(- Durable queue \(Kafka, SQS or Cloud Tasks\) with visibility timeouts. Messages carry an idempotency key) Tj T*
(  = sha256\(record_type + canonical_url\). Workers are stateless and horizontally scaled.) Tj T*
(- Per-source distributed token buckets live in Redis; aggregate request rate stays within each) Tj T*
(  publisher's published limit regardless of worker count. Per-domain semaphores become leased permits.) Tj T*
(- Checkpoints are committed per page/offset, as the arXiv PaperStore already does. At-least-once) Tj T*
(  delivery is safe because deduplication is deterministic on URL plus content hash.) Tj T*
(- Raw snapshots are written before parsing. Replay re-derives records from saved bytes and SHA-256) Tj T*
(  manifests, so an interrupted crawl resumes without re-fetching.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. 413 payload-too-large and 429 rate limit at thousands of concurrent extractions) Tj T*
(- The implemented engine chunks by UTF-8 bytes at paragraph boundaries, keeps every character, and) Tj T*
(  validates contiguous coverage. A provider 413 marks the chunk for halving and re-dispatch to the same) Tj T*
(  provider; smaller parts retain absolute character offsets.) Tj T*
(- A local request-size guard rejects an oversized body before it leaves the worker \(HTTPProvider) Tj T*
(  max_request_bytes\). Shrink factors are recorded per attempt, so chunk size adapts per provider/model.) Tj T*
(- 429 handling uses Retry-After when present, otherwise exponential backoff with uniform jitter,) Tj T*
(  bounded by attempts, a retry budget and a per-provider cooldown. Requests are serialized per provider) Tj T*
(  lock.) Tj T*
(- When the budget or cooldown is exceeded, the next provider in Gemini Flash -> Groq Llama 3 ->) Tj T*
(  DeepSeek is tried. Grounding validation is identical for every provider; a fallback cannot relax it.) Tj T*
(- At cluster scale, cooldowns live in Redis per provider/model, and a global token bucket prevents) Tj T*
(  thousands of workers from retrying in phase. 413/429 events are emitted as metrics and traces.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Freshness and distributed deduplication) Tj T*
(- Publication time comes only from structured fields \(RSS/Atom, JSON, meta tags, JSON-LD, Unix epochs\).) Tj T*
(  Naive timestamps are rejected rather than assumed UTC. Unknown or future dates are quarantined, never) Tj T*
(  backdated.) Tj T*
(- Freshness is evaluated at ingestion against the record's own collectedAt, so the 24-hour gate is) Tj T*
(  auditable later. Exported records store both published and ingested timestamps.) Tj T*
(- Three identities are claimed atomically: canonical URL, normalized content hash, and record-type) Tj T*
(  scoped identity. In production these are unique indexes and Redis SETNX claims keyed the same way, so) Tj T*
(  two workers cannot process the same article or job.) Tj T*
(- The processed registry is already a SQLite table keyed by \(identity_kind, identity, record_type\); it) Tj T*
(  maps directly to a partitioned Postgres table or DynamoDB key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Storage strategy) Tj T*
(- Primary operational database: PostgreSQL. Records, provenance, quarantine, entity mappings and crawl) Tj T*
(  checkpoints need transactions, uniqueness constraints and relational audits. Partition by month and) Tj T*
(  record type.) Tj T*
(- Raw object storage: S3/R2, partitioned source/date/run_id, with SHA-256 manifests and immutable) Tj T*
(  snapshots. Cheap, replayable, and the audit can re-hash every source.) Tj T*
(- Vector storage: Qdrant or pgvector for news/job/paper embeddings, sharded by record type. Used for) Tj T*
(  retrieval and related-content search, never as the source of truth for claims.) Tj T*
(- Graph storage: Neo4j or Postgres edge tables for entity, product and repository relationships.) Tj T*
(  Ownership edges carry evidence and a verification status; NAME_MATCH_ONLY edges are never promoted) Tj T*
(  silently.) Tj T*
(- Cache: Redis for robots policies, ETags, GitHub star TTLs and in-flight dedupe keys. Caches are) Tj T*
(  disposable; correctness never depends on them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Entity resolution) Tj T*
(- A 66-entity seed \(164 canonical names and aliases\) is normalized deterministically: NFKC, casefold,) Tj T*
ET
