(  punctuation to spaces, trailing legal suffix removal. Exact/alias lookup only; fuzzy similarity never) Tj T*
(  merges entities.) Tj T*
(- Conflicting aliases fail at load time. Duplicate entity IDs fail. Unknown names are preserved as) Tj T*
(  UNRESOLVED with a null canonical ID, and every mapping row retains raw name, normalized key, method,) Tj T*
(  source URL, source-text hash and evidence.) Tj T*
(- Resolution proves a name match, not ownership. The mapping log records ownership_verified=false and) Tj T*
(  NAME_MATCH_ONLY for every match. Product names and domains are never used to infer a company.) Tj T*
(- At scale, the alias index is a Postgres table plus a read-through cache; batch resolvers process 500k) Tj T*
(  names with the same deterministic function.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. LLM fallback, chunking, grounding and audit) Tj T*
(- Provider chain: Gemini Flash, Groq, DeepSeek. Every attempt records provider, model, status, latency,) Tj T*
(  chunk bytes, outcome, retry and available token usage; raw provider responses are saved without) Tj T*
(  credentials.) Tj T*
(- Each non-null claim must contain a verbatim quote with character offsets into the normalized source) Tj T*
(  text. Validation proves the quote exists at those offsets, the value occurs inside the quote, and the) Tj T*
(  quote sits inside one chunk.) Tj T*
(- Chunk spans must be contiguous and cover the full source. Invalid or ungrounded output is rejected) Tj T*
(  and never retried into a fabrication; the next provider may try with the same rules.) Tj T*
(- Phase III audit independently re-hashes the source and revalidates offsets. In the live run, 8/8) Tj T*
(  accepted claims revalidated; one provider response was rejected as ungrounded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Anti-bot compliance) Tj T*
(- Only documented APIs, RSS/Atom feeds, public datasets and robots-permitted HTML are used. robots.txt) Tj T*
(  is checked and cached per origin before article fetches; disallowed pages fall back to feed summaries) Tj T*
(  and are marked FEED_SUMMARY.) Tj T*
(- Per-domain concurrency caps, minimum spacing, retry budgets, circuit breakers and Retry-After) Tj T*
(  handling are implemented. Blocked, rate-limited and policy-restricted sources are logged in each) Tj T*
(  run's http_report.json.) Tj T*
(- Protected sources \(VentureBeat, Artificial Intelligence News, Datanami, Cloudflare/Datadome) Tj T*
(  directories, LinkedIn, Product Hunt\) are documented for official API, partnership, data-export or) Tj T*
(  manual-review access. No stealth, proxy rotation or challenge-solving capability exists or is) Tj T*
(  claimed.) Tj T*
(- Playwright is not required for the selected structured sources and is not used. Browser rendering) Tj T*
(  would be introduced only for a permitted, genuinely JavaScript-rendered source.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Observability, alerting, failure recovery and quality gates) Tj T*
(- Metrics per source: request rate, success/error rate, p95 latency, retries, 429s, robots blocks,) Tj T*
(  circuit opens, records/s, quarantine rate, freshness rejections and grounding failures.) Tj T*
(- Alerts on circuit-open, sustained 429s, zero-fresh sources, schema-validation spikes, ungrounded-) Tj T*
(  output spikes and any failed audit gate. Traces carry run_id and idempotency key.) Tj T*
(- Failure recovery: at-least-once queue, idempotent writes, checkpoint resume, dead-letter queue with) Tj T*
(  status and attempt history, and raw-snapshot replay. Quarantine is a first-class output, not an error) Tj T*
(  swallow.) Tj T*
(- Publication gates: Phase I minimum counts and provenance; Phase II source coverage and 24-hour) Tj T*
(  freshness; Phase III grounding; Phase IV seed/determinism/ownership; Phase V compliance. A failed) Tj T*
(  gate blocks export.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Implemented vs designed) Tj T*
(Implemented and executed locally: dataset acquisitions \(4,656 startups, 24,938 products, 1,790 papers,) Tj T*
(1,660 accepted paper-repo associations with live stars\), 6 news feeds and 8 job boards with 24-hour) Tj T*
(gating \(18 news, 124 jobs\), 3 live LLM extractions with 8 grounded claims and provider fallback,) Tj T*
(66-entity resolution with 4,782 mapping rows, robots/retry/circuit-breaker controls, and these audits.) Tj T*
(Designed but not executed at scale: distributed queue/workers, Redis rate coordination,) Tj T*
(PostgreSQL/object/vector/graph partitioning, 500k-record load test, dead-letter automation and) Tj T*
(production alerting. This document makes no throughput claim for those components.) Tj T*
